lowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The code looks good, save for one small observation, since the slot is unused there shouldn't be any collision with RIDs in *this* owner\r\n\r\nThe one risk would be collisions *between* owners, but I think we can consider that risk pretty negligible, we might want to look at some way to reduce the potential impact of that\r\n\r\nSome things I think we should consider:\r\n* Making this configurable with a compile flag, to restore the crash\r\n* Still evaluate areas in the engine where we should reuse RIDs better, to improve general performance and avoid unnecessary allocating and freeing\r\n\r\nBut generally the code looks valid, and the `owns` check should work correctly as `0x7FFFFFFF` is now a valid case\r\n\r\nSo I think we can continue to evaluate other improvements down the line, but I think this is good as it is","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105538#pullrequestreview-2779950760","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105538","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105538#pullrequestreview-2779950760"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105538"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-19T12:27:04Z","commit_id":"c6c06a966a1c8d9feecd17692937ae36179cc774"}]